Delete one or more empty Kafka consumer groups.

Usage:
  confluent kafka consumer group delete <group-1> [group-2] ... [group-n] [flags]

Examples:
Delete the consumer group "my-group". The group must have no active members.

  $ confluent kafka consumer group delete my-group

Flags:
      --kafka-endpoint string   Endpoint to be used for this Kafka cluster.
      --force                   Skip the deletion confirmation prompt.
      --cluster string          Kafka cluster ID.
      --context string          CLI context name.
      --environment string      Environment ID.

Global Flags:
  -h, --help            Show help for this command.
      --unsafe-trace    Equivalent to -vvvv, but also log HTTP requests and responses which might contain plaintext secrets.
  -v, --verbose count   Increase verbosity (-v for warn, -vv for info, -vvv for debug, and -vvvv for trace).
